--- !u!114 &703678451
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 703678449}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6ba2ac043a0776a4d846aaf6ba38a734, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: lathe's tool turret
  description: 'This is a lathe''s tool turret.


    A lathe''s tool turret is a
    device that holds multiple cutting tools and automatically switches between them.
    This allows for the continuous and diverse machining of a wheel. It eliminates
    the need for an operator to manually change tools, which shortens processing
    time and improves productivity.


    Functions of a Tool Turret

    A tool
    turret enables the following operations:


    Outer and Inner Diameter Cutting:
    Precisely cuts the outer rim and inner hub bore of the wheel.


    Facing: Uses
    a tool to smooth the circular end face, such as the wheel''s mounting surface.


    Grooving:
    Switches to a different tool to cut specific grooves for a wheel''s design or
    function.


    Drilling: Attaches a drill tool to create the center bore or
    other holes in the wheel.


    Threading: Replaces the tool to cut screw threads
    into the wheel''s hub bore.


    Advantages of a Tool Turret

    The main advantage
    of a tool turret is its automatic tool changing capability. By using multiple
    tools on a single machine, it offers the following benefits:


    Improved Work
    Efficiency: Multiple steps can be performed in a single setup, which significantly
    reduces production time.


    High-Precision Finishing: The lack of tool-changing
    errors ensures consistent quality during machining.


    Handling Complex Shapes:
    By combining multiple tools, a single machine can finish wheels with diverse
    and complex shapes.'
  type: 0
  url: 
