  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6ba2ac043a0776a4d846aaf6ba38a734, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: End Mill
  description: 'This is an end mill part from milling machine.


    An end mill
    is a versatile cutting tool used for a variety of tasks, including milling surfaces,
    cutting grooves, drilling holes, and machining contours.


    Mounted on a milling
    machine, the end mill rotates at high speed and is fed into the workpiece (in
    this case, a wheel). It gradually carves away material to create the desired
    shape.


    Examples of Machining with an End Mill

    Milling a Flat Surface:
    It precisely smooths the wheel''s mounting surface.


    Groove Machining: It
    carves grooves for design or function, such as between the spokes or creating
    decorative recesses.


    Hole Drilling: It drills cylindrical holes, like those
    for wheel nuts.


    This tool is unique because it has cutting edges on both
    its cylindrical side and its tip, allowing it to machine in multiple directions.
    Its versatility makes it one of the most fundamental cutting tools used with
    a milling machine.'
  type: 0
  url: 
