  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6ba2ac043a0776a4d846aaf6ba38a734, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: chuck, wheel holder from lathe
  description: 'The part of a lathe that holds the wheel is called a chuck.

    This
    is a chuck part from lathe.



    For a wheel, a specialized type of chuck is
    used. This is a 3-jaw chuck, which uses a set of jaws to grip the workpiece firmly.
    These jaws can be adjusted to accommodate different sizes of wheels.





    3-jaw
    chuck: This is a self-centering chuck where all three jaws move simultaneously.
    It is quick and easy to set up for round workpieces like wheels.'
  type: 0
  url: 
